nvdisplay: gpu_t234d_kernel: T194 name and address width

Change the GPU name string to "T194" and keep the physical address width
at 39 bits (Xavier uses 40-bit PA space, 39 bits for system memory -
same as Orin).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform-specific]
Signed-off-by: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>
--- a/nvdisplay/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/gpu_t234d_kernel.c
+++ b/nvdisplay/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/gpu_t234d_kernel.c
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@
     void *nameStringBuffer
 )
 {
-    const char name[] = "T234D";
+    const char name[] = "T194";
     const NvU32 inputLength = NV2080_GPU_MAX_NAME_STRING_LENGTH;
 
     if (type == NV2080_CTRL_GPU_GET_NAME_STRING_FLAGS_TYPE_ASCII)
